  data: {
    LLM: 'Four players in two partnerships bid 5 to 9 for the right to choose trump. The 6 of the chosen trump suit is highest; then all Kings, Queens, and Jacks in suit order (clubs, spades, hearts, diamonds), then trump suit A-10-9-8-7. Left of dealer leads; must follow suit and must beat the current trick if able. First team to 16 strokes wins.',
    Player: 'Four players in two partnerships bid 5 to 9 for the right to choose trump. The 6 of the chosen trump suit is highest; then all Kings, Queens, and Jacks in suit order (clubs, spades, hearts, diamonds), then trump suit A-10-9-8-7. Left of dealer leads; must follow suit and must beat the current trick if able. First team to 16 strokes wins.',
    objective: 'Score at least 61 points (out of 120 card points) to win the round.',
    gameplay: 'Four players in two partnerships bid 5 to 9 for the right to choose trump. The 6 of the chosen trump suit is highest; then all Kings, Queens, and Jacks in suit order (clubs, spades, hearts, diamonds), then trump suit A-10-9-8-7. Left of dealer leads; must follow suit and must beat the current trick if able. First team to 16 strokes wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Follow suit; picture cards (J, Q, K) count as trumps.',
      'Must trump if void in led suit; must beat highest card in trick if able.',
      '61+ card points wins the round; 16 strokes win the game.',
      'Tie at 60: redeal same trumps, no bidding. All pass: diamonds, winners score 1 stroke.',
    ],
